    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="1765" n="1660" xml:id="pg1660"/>

                <head>467. Telegram Supnu 433 From Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d467-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-05-14T19:00:00+01:00">May 14, 1959, 7
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d467-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d467-1"/>
                <p>Supnu 433. Following is text memorandum worked out ad referendum at US–UK staff
                    level after Gromyko-Herter-Lloyd meeting reported separately.</p>
                <p>“The Foreign Ministers of the USSR, UK, and USA have exchanged views on the
                    position reached in the Conf for the Discontinuance of Nuclear Weapons Tests.
                    The three FonMins recognised that technical aspects of questions outstanding at
                    the conf require further study. The three FonMins agreed that their technical
                    representatives should meet in Geneva on June 1, 1959 to consider, in the light
                    of the most recent scientific and technical information available: <list>
                        <label>I.</label>
                        <item>Recommendations for techniques for detecting nuclear explosions at
                            altitudes above 50 kilometres and in outer space;</item>
                        <label>II.</label>
                        <item>Recommendations for improving methods of distinguishing between
                            underground explosions and earthquakes;</item>
                        <label>III.</label>
                        <item>Recommendations for specific technical criteria which must be
                            satisfied by data from the control system before an inspection can be
                            undertaken.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The three FonMins agreed that their technical representatives should be requested
                    to report to the Conf for the <pb facs="d467-2" n="2" type="facsimile"
                        xml:id="d467-2"/> Discontinuance of Nuclear Weapon Tests at the earliest
                    possible date, and in any case to make an interim report to the Conf when it
                    resumes its meetings on June 8 1959.”</p>
                <p>Since USDel technical staff other than Northrup has left, request Dept comments
                    on suggested terms of reference in time to allow transmittal above text to Sov
                    Del tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Above has not yet been seen by Secretary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Villard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
